  "narrative": "The feature_002 disentanglement batch strongly supports large, threshold-sized conditional dataset associations for the three accepted markers. feature_002=1 versus 0 remains large and precise within feature_010=0 (R54 signed 0.780, interval 0.719 to 0.841) and feature_010=1 (R55 signed 0.857, interval 0.755 to 0.960), and within feature_037=0 (R58 signed 0.809, interval 0.749 to 0.869) and feature_037=1 (R59 signed 0.790, interval 0.661 to 0.920). Most importantly, it remains large among samples lacking both feature_010 and feature_037 (R62 signed 0.784, interval 0.736 to 0.833). Symmetrically, feature_010=1 versus 0 remains large within feature_002=0 (R56 signed 0.800, interval 0.744 to 0.857) and feature_002=1 (R57 signed 0.878, interval 0.773 to 0.982), and the accepted negative feature_037 contrast remains large within feature_002=0 (R60 signed 0.796, interval 0.739 to 0.853) and feature_002=1 (R61 signed 0.814, interval 0.684 to 0.945). Therefore I accept H58-H66 as threshold-sized conditional descriptive associations in the supplied dataset. These results make simple pairwise proxy or full-redundancy interpretations less plausible, but they do not prove causal independence, mechanistic separability, multivariable noncollinearity, or generalizability.\n\nThe feature_002 interactions with feature_010 and feature_037 do not support threshold-sized effect modification. The feature_002-by-feature_010 interaction is directionally positive but small and imprecise around zero (R64 signed 0.077, interval -0.042 to 0.196), so I reject H68 despite the upper bound crossing the 0.15-unit threshold because the evidence does not establish a meaningful positive interaction. The feature_002-by-feature_037 interaction is small and near zero (R65 signed -0.018, interval -0.161 to 0.124), and H69 is rejected and closed. Because H53 is now supported by its own discovery, independent validation, and a persistent conditional battery including a triple-marker-absent feature_002 residual test, I close H53 while retaining it as an accepted dataset association.\n\nThe feature_003 residual after excluding feature_010, feature_037, and feature_002 (H67) remains borderline and scientifically informative. R63 gives a signed estimate of 0.144 in the claimed negative-raw direction, with a precise-looking interval 0.083 to 0.204. The point estimate is just below the 0.15-unit threshold, the interval excludes zero, and the upper bound exceeds threshold. This is not enough to accept, but it is not the same as the broader non-significant or lower-bound-negative borderline feature_003 comparisons that were rejected earlier. Given repeated direction-consistent feature_003 signals, I keep H67 unresolved and request independent validation to decide whether this dominant-marker-absent feature_003 contrast is genuinely near threshold. I do not treat the current evidence as evidence of causality, biological mechanism, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 5 appraise: H58-H66 all accepted and closed. The conditional battery shows feature_002, feature_010, and feature_037 each retain large descriptive associations in strata defined by the other markers, and feature_002 retains a large association when feature_010 and feature_037 are absent (R62 signed 0.784). Thus the three markers are not pairwise redundant in a simple conditional-descriptive sense. H53 can be closed as accepted and validated. H68/H69 feature_002 interactions are rejected: H68 estimate 0.077, interval -0.042 to 0.196; H69 estimate -0.018, interval -0.161 to 0.124.\n\nFeature_003 remains the main borderline line. H67 among feature_010=0, feature_037=0, feature_002=0 gives signed estimate 0.1438, interval 0.083 to 0.204; below threshold at point estimate but interval crosses threshold. I requested validation of H67. In synthesis, reassess H67 immediately when validation arrives and explicitly decide whether to accept only if the validated interval supports a threshold-sized feature_003 contrast in this residual cell, otherwise reject or close as near-threshold unresolved depending on interval. Do not accept feature_003 solely because interval includes threshold.\n\nNext analyses should run active H70-H80: triple/co-occurrence residual tests for feature_010, feature_037, feature_002, plus feature_003-by-feature_002 interaction H79 and broad feature_033 screen H80. If H79 is null, strengthen closure of marker-dependent feature_003 explanations. If H80 is threshold and precise, register follow-up conditional tests before validation. Keep claims dataset-only; no causality, mechanism, or generalizability.",
